    "title": "House of the Week: Brick-front contemporary in Castleton - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Shannon Fromma ,\n13 hours ago House of the Week: 1336 Partridge Drive, Castleton (Meri Coons/Meri Light Photography) This week’s selection is a distinctive brick-front, three-level contemporary retreat on over two-and-a-half private acres in the East Greenbush Central School District. Built in 1995, 1336 Patridge Drive is located in an established neighborhood not far from I-90 and is accessed via a long, secluded driveway. The home offers 3,500 square feet of living space with three full bathrooms and five bedrooms, including a spacious primary suite on the main level. The chef’s kitchen boasts high-end appliances, granite countertops and space for entertaining, while the family room showcases soaring cathedral ceilings and a dramatic stone fireplace. Sunlight fills the heated sunroom, complete with a vaulted wood-trimmed ceiling and views of the private backyard, deck, fire pit and heated in-ground pool. Additional features include a finished basement, three-car garage and numerous recent upgrades, including a new roof, updated heating and central air, carpeting and fencing.\nList price: $879,900. Taxes: $14,000. To learn more about this property, contact Judi Gabler with Gabler Realty, LLC at 518-278-7230.\nHouse of the Week: 1336 Partridge Drive, Castleton (Meri Coons/Meri Light Photography) Sign up for Times Union newsletters here\nRead the original article on timesunion.com",
